# Meta Display Web Apps

This repo builds standalone Web Apps for Meta Ray-Ban Display glasses. Before changing app code, re-read the canonical docs and call Wearables MCP `search_webapps_docs` when that tool is available. If MCP is unavailable, use the docs below and say so.

## Canonical docs (source of truth)

- https://wearables.developer.meta.com/docs/develop/webapps
- https://wearables.developer.meta.com/docs/develop/webapps/setup/
- https://wearables.developer.meta.com/docs/develop/webapps/build/
- https://wearables.developer.meta.com/docs/develop/webapps/test/
- https://developers.meta.com/blog/build-for-display-glasses/
- Toolkit: https://github.com/facebookincubator/meta-wearables-webapp
- MCP: https://mcp.developer.meta.com/wearables (`search_webapps_docs`, no auth)

If a plugin skill conflicts with those pages, follow the official docs.

## Hard constraints

- Fixed **600 x 600** viewport, `overflow: hidden`, no page scrolling
- Additive display: page background `#000000` (transparent). Visible UI uses dark gray (`#1C1E21`), light high-contrast text
- Input is **arrow keys + Enter** (Neural Band / captouch). No mouse, touch, or physical keyboard. Every control needs `.focusable` and a visible focus state
- Required HTML: `meta name="mrbd-web-app-capable" content="yes"`, app-specific `description`, PNG favicon ≥52x52 (no SVG)
- Glasses load **HTTPS only**. Host on **GitHub Pages**, not Vercel. Localhost is for desktop smoke tests only
- Public URLs: `https://ggoonnzzaallo.github.io/meta_display/` (launcher) and `.../apps/<name>/` (keep the trailing slash)
- Default stack: vanilla HTML/CSS/JS in `apps/<name>/`. Register each new app in root `app.js` `APPS`. Do not add React/Vue unless the user asks
- Situation ingest: `scripts/fetch_feed.py` writes `apps/situation/feed.json` in the Pages job. Do not fetch third-party RSS from the glasses Web App.
- Markets ingest: `scripts/fetch_markets.py` writes `apps/markets/feed.json` (Yahoo quotes for movers, Nasdaq earnings, WSJ/CNBC/SA/BBC headlines). Do not scrape Finviz.

## Not supported yet (official build guide)

Camera, microphone, text input, offline, notifications, back navigation, continuous cursor.
